Universal Claude Code policies for all of my projects.

These are user-scope rules: they load into context at the start of every
Claude Code session, in every repository, ordered before any project rules
so a project can always override them.

Install (local machine):
    git clone git@github.com:idonov8/claude-policies.git ~/.claude/rules

Install (cloud sessions) — add to your cloud environment's setup script:
    git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/idonov8/claude-policies.git ~/.claude/rules

Update:
    git -C ~/.claude/rules pull

Conventions:
- One topic per file. Keep each well under 200 lines.
- Only policies that hold for *every* project belong here. Anything that
  names a path, a command, or a framework belongs in that repo's CLAUDE.md.
- This file has no .md extension on purpose: every .md here is loaded as a
  rule, and a readme in context is wasted tokens.
- To scope a rule to certain files, add `paths:` frontmatter so it only
  loads when Claude opens a match.
